GROWTH GAPS

1. High-Value Case Studies and Serialized Frameworks:
Competitors like @dhavalkataria_ structure their content into episodic series (such as Un-Broke-ing India) with clear step-by-step business execution frameworks. Garvit currently focuses on tool hacks (such as free Claude tokens and alternate platforms) without connecting them to a broader, highly engaging narrative framework that drives massive view durations and saves.

2. Professional Positioning and Production Quality:
Top creators like @arshman and @nick_saraev use polished hooks that immediately call out industry standards and specific target audiences (such as vibe-coded apps and e-commerce founders). Garvit's casual conversational openings in Hinglish work well for community trust, but lack the authoritative visual and verbal framing that commands higher algorithmic reach and broader shareability among non-niche tech users.

3. Automated Lead Capture and Resource Distribution:
Competitors utilize direct comment-to-DM triggers paired with high-perceived-value deliverables (like comprehensive codebases, security plugins, or curated prompt PDFs) to artificially spike comment velocity. While Garvit leverages comment triggers, scaling the upfront hook to promise a singular, definitive asset will bridge the gap between high comment counts and wider explore-page distribution.


RECOMMENDED ACTIONS

1. Adopt the Episodic Series Format:
Launch a 3-part serialized series over the next 7 days focusing on a single high-impact outcome, such as building and deploying a complete AI SaaS product completely for free using open-source tokens, mirroring the high retention structure seen in successful competitor series.

2. Upgrade Hook Architecture for Technical Content:
Revise the first 3 seconds of upcoming Reels to directly call out specific developer pain points or high-value financial thresholds (for example: "How to get 9 billion free AI tokens without hitting subscription limits"), removing casual filler words to increase average watch time.

3. Optimize Posting Schedule Alignment:
Schedule all content releases strictly between 6:00 PM and 9:00 PM IST to match peak audience activity windows and maximize initial engagement velocity for the first 60 minutes post-publish.
